"""Checks for the metered cloud billing extract.

The checks carry their own copy of the shipped extract and of twenty other extracts in
the same layout. Each of those extracts has its own kinds, kind weights, cancellation
table, rate card, figures and withdrawal journal; the expected values of every extract
are derived here by a reference of the checks' own, which settles each extract's
configuration from its evidence. Submitted code runs only as an unprivileged subprocess,
in its own session, with a timeout, under an interpreter that sees only the standard
library, with an audit hook that records every file it opens and every module it
imports. Its cost is measured from this process as child CPU time, never by anything the
submission prints.

Negative checks return True when the failure they name happened; their negative weight
does the punishing.
"""

